// Title: Linux Base64 Encoded Shebang In CLI
// Sigma ID: fe2f9663-41cb-47e2-b954-8a228f3b9dff
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-15 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1140
// Description: Detects the presence of a base64 version of the shebang in the commandline, which could indicate
//   a malicious payload about to be decoded
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://www.trendmicro.com/pl_pl/research/20/i/the-evolution-of-malicious-shell-scripts.html
//   - https://github.com/carlospolop/PEASS-ng/tree/master/linPEAS
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_base64_shebang_cli.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "IyEvYmluL2Jhc2" or ProcessCommandLine contains "IyEvYmluL2Rhc2" or ProcessCommandLine contains "IyEvYmluL3pza" or ProcessCommandLine contains "IyEvYmluL2Zpc2" or ProcessCommandLine contains "IyEvYmluL3No"
